From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOTTY Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:30:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] hottyterm: a document that scrolls takes the wheel
 first
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SPEC §5.3 (hotty f171655): a document that asks to scroll (a=doc
scroll=1, 2 or 3) scrolls as a page does, and a wheel, a touchpad's
scroll or a touch drag over it is its own while something in it can move
that way. Where nothing can, it goes on to the terminal as over the cells
(§9), unless overscroll-behavior stops it. hotty-blitz decides, through
its new hotty_host_wheel (hotty-blitz C ABI: hotty_host_wheel and
hotty_host_end_gesture are new): it returns whether the surface took the
gesture.

Surface.scrollCallback now hands the wheel to surfaceScroll first, which
finds the surface under the pointer as a press does (passing through
where it takes no pointer, §9.3) and turns Ghostty's offsets into
hotty-blitz's: pixels, positive right and down, a notch as many pixels as
it scrolls the cells (mouse-scroll-multiplier included). A wheel it does
not take goes on to scrollback, mouse reports or alternate scroll as
before. Over the cells, or while the program holds the pointer, the
gesture is the terminal's, even where it goes on over a surface.

Scrolling shows overlay scrollbars that fade, so key and pointer events
now set the frame timer after they render, as the stream does.

Upstream files: src/Surface.zig, 2 lines (a hook and its comment).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
